{"id": 19, "ts": 1780501448.270444, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I agree with James that Candidate\u202fA remains our strongest option.\u202fWhile we still lack direct evidence of his stress\u2011resilience and decision\u2011making under pressure, his proven ability to anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, and his excellent spatial vision give us confidence in his technical competence and situational awareness\u2014key for long\u2011distance flights.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fB\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation record is problematic (\u201ccan be uncooperative\u201d and \u201cgrumpy\u201d), which could jeopardize cockpit harmony, and we have no data on his professional communication.\u202fCandidate\u202fC, despite quick decision\u2011making, struggles with communication and is seen as egocentric, raising concerns for crew interaction.\u202fCandidate\u202fD shows adequate response to unexpected events but we have no concrete evidence of stress\u2011resilience or crew cooperation, and his moodiness and loner reputation further weaken his fit.\u202fGiven the balance of strengths and weaknesses, A\u2019s leadership and safety\u2011focused traits outweigh his interpersonal drawbacks, so I continue to vote for Candidate\u202fA."}
