{"id": 38, "ts": 1780501598.2130015, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fA is our best choice. As Sarah and Emily have noted, his ability to anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, and his excellent spatial vision give him a clear edge in operational reliability and technical competence for long\u2011distance flights. His very good leadership further supports crew cooperation and responsibility. While we lack direct observations of his stress\u2011resilience, the proactive hazard anticipation indicates he would manage pressure effectively. The alternative candidates each have more serious deficits: B is uncooperative and grumpy; C is egocentric with communication difficulties; D has a hot temper and is seen as a know\u2011it\u2011all. Even though A can be a show\u2011off and is not very open to new ideas, these concerns are outweighed by his safety\u2011focused strengths. Therefore, I continue to vote for Candidate\u202fA."}
